messages.reasoning_content:
Core components have been created. Next, build the 01_Home frame. This is a big one. Let's plan the layout:

01_Home (width 1440):
- Header (instance)
- Hero: Photo_Hero full-width background, with a center-aligned card containing "New Arrival", "Discover Our New Collection", description text, and BUY NOW button
- Browse The Range section: title, subtitle, 3 tiles (Dining, Living, Bedroom) with photos
- Our Products: title, 8 product cards (4 columns × 2 rows), Leviosa card in hover state, Show More button
- Inspiration section: "50+ Beautiful rooms inspiration", copy, Explore More, slides: Photo_Inspiration_Inner_Peace (current, with "01 — Bed Room", "Inner Peace", open arrow), next Photo_Inspiration_2, Photo_Inspiration_3, next chevron, slide indicator 4 dots with current being 1
- Share your setup: "Share your setup with" "#FurniroFurniture", Photo_Setup_1..9
- Footer

Product card data: need to set name/description/price/old price/badge/photo per card. Create a helper that clones the ProductCard instance and overrides text and photo. Photo override: the instance contains a Photo instance (of Photo_Product_Leviosa). To swap the photo, can we use instance.swapComponent? The Photo inside the card is an instance of a media component. We can use swapComponent(newComponent). Media components are components on page 04, so swapComponent should work.

Badge: hide if null (visible=false), set color to sale or new (neu teal), set text.

OldPrice: hide if null.

Let's write a helper function to customize card instances.

Home layout details:
- Hero: height ~600. Photo_Hero as background (1440x600, cropped). Center-aligned white card (width ~600) with "New Arrival" (small gold), "Discover Our New Collection" (40 bold), description text, BUY NOW button (gold).
- Browse The Range: padding 64, title center-aligned "Browse The Range" (32 bold), subtitle "Find the right pieces for every room in your home.", 3 tiles: each tile has a photo (360x400?) with a label card at the bottom. Tile width: (1312-2*32)/3 ≈ 416. Photo_Range_Dining/Living/Bedroom.
- Our Products: title "Our Products" center-aligned, grid 4 columns × 2 rows, gap 32: card width 280 → 4*280+3*32=1216, fits within 1312 with padding 64. Actually 1312-1216=96, so use gap 32 and center-align. Show More button (outline gold).
- Inspiration: cream background section. Left: "50+ Beautiful rooms inspiration" (40 bold, width ~500), copy, "Explore More" button. Right: slides — current slide is a large card (Photo_Inspiration_Inner_Peace ~372x520?) with an overlay box "01 — Bed Room", "Inner Peace", open arrow icon (gold circle with Icon_Arrow_Right). Next to it: Photo_Inspiration_2, Photo_Inspiration_3 smaller, next chevron button, indicator dots (4, current is 1).
- Share your setup: "Share your setup with" center-aligned, "#FurniroFurniture" gold, 9 setup photos in a row (each ~140x140 cropped).
- Footer.

Frame height: auto (vertical auto layout, hug). Build the frame as a vertical auto layout with width fixed at 1440, height auto.

Let's write the code for 01_Home. It's long, so watch out for the 50000 character limit — should be fine.

Helper for card customization:

async function cardInst(idx, hover){
  const comp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(hover?ids.pch:ids.pc);
  const i = comp.createInstance();
  const p = prods[idx];
  // swap photo
  const photo = i.findOne(n=>n.name==='Photo');
  const newPhotoComp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(p[5]);
  photo.swapComponent(newPhotoComp);
  photo.resize(280,280);
  // badge
  const badge = i.findOne(n=>n.name==='Badge');
  if(p[4]){ badge.visible=true; badge.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:p[4]==='New'?C.neu:C.sale}]; badge.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT').characters=p[4]; }
  else badge.visible=false;
  // texts
  i.findOne(n=>n.name==='Name').characters=p[0];
  i.findOne(n=>n.name==='Desc').characters=p[1];
  i.findOne(n=>n.name==='Price').characters=p[2];
  const op=i.findOne(n=>n.name==='OldPrice');
  if(p[3]){op.visible=true;op.characters=p[3];}else op.visible=false;
  return i;
}

Note: swapping text characters on an instance requires loading the font — already loaded.

Also, need to save ids globally. Since each use_figma call is separate, save ids to pluginData? setPluginData is prohibited ("MUST NEVER use ... setPluginData"). Hmm, the tool description says never use loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync. So I have to return ids and pass them manually between calls. I have the ids from the previous call: header 19:20, footer 19:48, featureStrip 19:77, pageTitle 19:86, productCard 19:98, productCardHover 19:126, pagination 19:138.

Also, need to check whether the previous failed run left partial nodes behind (the first two attempts errored out midway — did the nodes persist? The error occurred at line 80 during the header build. Nodes created before the error may remain on the page). Should clean up stray frames. Let's check the page's children first and delete anything that isn't a component we created. Actually, the first failed attempt created a header component (figma.createComponent) and some frames. The second attempt failed at line 80 (fs counterAxisAlignItem) — created header frame, footer, etc. as regular frames. These stray nodes exist. Let's list the page's children and delete anything not in our ids list.

Next, build 01_Home. Let's write the code.

Hero: use Photo_Hero instance resized to 1440x600? The original Photo_Hero is 343x240 (component). Resizing the instance to 1440x600 will stretch it. That's fine ("photos can be freely cropped" — stretching is not cropping, but acceptable. Better to keep aspect ratio and crop with a clipped frame). To crop: create a wrapper frame 1440x600 with clipsContent, place the instance scaled to cover: scale = max(1440/343, 600/240)=max(4.2,2.5)=4.2 → 1440x1008, y offset -(1008-600)/2=-204. This preserves aspect ratio. Let's write a helper coverPhoto(id,w,h).

Inspiration slide: current slide card ~372x520: photo cover + overlay info box at bottom-left: white/85 box with "01 — Bed Room" (small gold), "Inner Peace" (24 bold), gold circle with white arrow icon.

Next slide: Photo_Inspiration_2 (162x240) → display at ~200x520? Original ratio 162:240. Use cover crop at 200x520. Photo_Inspiration_3 similarly. Next chevron: circular button.

Indicator: 4 dots, current is gold and larger.

Setup photos: 9 photos in a row: total width 1312, gap 16 → each (1312-8*16)/9 ≈ 131.8 → 132x132 cover crop.

Range tiles: width 416, photo height 400, label overlay at bottom: white box with title (Dining/Living/Bedroom) + small "Explore Now"? The required list only asks for the name and photo. Keep it simple: photo with a gradient-ish label bar at the bottom. Place a white semi-transparent label box at the bottom-left with the name.

Section order per the required list (alphabetical, layout is up to me): Header, Hero, Browse The Range, Our Products, Inspiration, Share your setup, Footer.

Buttons: reuse the given Button component (1:23) for BUY NOW / Show More / Explore More? The brief says to reuse the default Button from 02·Components. Button component: 222x74, white text "Button", gold border, no fill. Can create an instance and override the text to "BUY NOW" etc. For a primary gold-filled button, we can set the instance's fill (instance fill overrides are allowed) and border. Let's use instances of 1:23 with overrides: text characters, fill gold, stroke gold. This demonstrates reuse.

Show More: outline style — instance with text "Show More", stroke gold, text gold.

OK, let's write the code for 01_Home. Also, clean up stray nodes first.

Frame: create a frame named '01_Home', layoutMode VERTICAL, width 1440, height auto (primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO), fill white, itemSpacing 0, counterAxisSizingMode FIXED.

Position: place at x=0, y=0 on the workspace page.

Sections as plain frames (not components, except for the reusable ones). The brief says to build business components as reusable components — Header/Footer/FeatureStrip/PageTitle/ProductCard/Pagination are components. Section-level stuff can be frames. That's enough, but "all other states, header, footer, navigation, and all business components as reusable components" — product card, header, footer, pagination are covered. Could also componentize the breadcrumb, but the PageTitle component covers that.

Let's write the code. It's long, so split it up: first cleanup + 01_Home.

